{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1555119-how-would-the-gudthabak-explain-how-their-bull-blooded-all-have-wolf-themed-tells","id":1555119,"title":"How would the Gudthabak explain how their \"bull-blooded\" all have wolf themed tells?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-11-05T08:29:34-08:00","id":1555119,"title":"How would the Gudthabak explain how their \"bull-blooded\" all have wolf themed tells?","content":"So we all know the Bull-Shifters steal wolf-blooded and transform them into bull-shifters. They also probably have some brainwashed wolfblooded families who think they are bull-blooded. How would one explain how their kin's tells are mostly wolf-themed and not bull-themed? When a &quot;bull&quot;-blooded is born in the community with a wolf pelt for a siblings what's the party line, &quot;You have a very deformed bull pelt sibling.&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","user":"Snailslayer","date":". 11-05-2025, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T18:53:44-08:00","id":1555150,"title":"","content":"Not all Tells are wolf-themed, the Gudthabak don't increase their numbers by breeding, wolf-blooded families patronized by them don't necessarily know the nature of the distinction by which they have their gods' favor, and going back to <i>War Against the Pure</i> the bull-shifters are pointed to new prospects by Helions. A family whose children are often &quot;daughters of the wolf&quot; (to use the corebook's distinction)need not worry about explaining the occasional overt physical mutation or strangeness of the sort demonstrated by &quot;sons of the moon.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-06T00:10:33-08:00","id":1555155,"title":"","content":"I could easily see some of the responses being brutal. Born with a living pelt? Living pelts can be tossed in a fire pretty easily. Born with big, sharp teeth? Can go to a dentist to have them torn out and replaced.<br /> <br /> Depends on the community. Some might be more brutal than that. Some &quot;nicer&quot; Baal-Hadad communities might nip the problem in the bud by having those wolf-blooded fast-tracked for the Rite of Molech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-07T07:32:38-08:00","id":1555203,"title":"","content":"What book are the Gudthabak from? They sound really interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":""